Law enforcement and governments use a variety of methods to detect and track drug money laundering operations. These include monitoring financial transactions, analyzing large data sets, investigating suspicious activity reports (SARs), and using specialized financial intelligence units. To counter these measures, money laundering operations can use strategies such as utilizing shell companies and offshore accounts, layering transactions through multiple accounts or countries, using bulk cash payments or prepaid cards instead of checks or electronic transfers, and maintaining good record keeping practices. Furthermore, it is important for law enforcement agencies to stay up-to-date with the latest technological advances in order to remain effective at detecting money laundering activities. 
